/target

# The index cache. `docs/index-design.md` puts it inside the project on purpose — it travels with a
# checkout so CI gets the same warm cache as a developer — but it is derived data, so it never belongs in
# a commit. Deleting it is always safe: every entry is rebuilt from the file it describes.
.cppls/

# Backups and reports written while repairing this folder's Windows permissions. They are the rollback for a
# change to an access-control list, which is a fact about one machine and not about the project — so they stay
# on the machine that needed them. The folder is safe to delete once the write failures it describes are gone.
.dsh-acl-recovery/
